    {
      "text": "land was not able to bear them, Gen. 13:6. Sarah, that is ninety years old, bear, Gen. 17:17. I have born him a son in his old age, Gen. 21:7. shalt not bear false witness, Ex. 20:16 (Deut. 5:20; Matt. 19:18; Mark 10:19; Luke 18:20; Rom. 13:9). Aaron may bear the iniquity, Ex. 28:38. goat shall bear … all their iniquities, Lev. 16:22. children shall … bear your whoredoms, Num. 14:33. thy sons and thy father’s house … shall bear the iniquity, Num. 18:1. I am not able to bear you myself alone, Deut. 1:9. thy God bare thee, as a man doth bear his son, Deut. 1:31. earth … I bear up the pillars of it, Ps. 75:3. They shall bear thee up in their hands, Ps. 91:12 (Matt. 4:6; Luke 4:11). wounded spirit who can bear, Prov. 18:14. They bear him upon the shoulder, Isa. 46:7. Surely he hath borne our griefs, Isa. 53:4 (Mosiah 14:4). he shall bear their iniquities, Isa. 53:11 (Mosiah 14:11). he bare the sin of many, and made intercession, Isa. 53:12 (Mosiah 14:12). Lord could no longer bear, because of the evil, Jer. 44:22. That thou mayest bear thine own shame, Ezek. 16:54. son shall not bear the iniquity of the father, Ezek. 18:20.",
